I just noticed something that has me puzzled . . .  I found an
an altar at a nice early level, so decided to hang about for a
while to see what I could wheedle out of my god (I'm lawful so
I'm looking for Mjolly 8).  At one point I was attacked (while
standing on the altar) by four carnivorous apes.  Not too big a
deal, I'm already level 10 and have snickersnee so I dispatch
them easily enough.  Then comes the fun part, sacrificing them to
see what goodies I'll get.  I had recently prayed, so I figured
four ape corpses should help more than a bit.  The first two said
something about having a hopeful feeling, then the third one said
nothing (other than it disappeared) then the fourth one (all of
these are one right after the other, nothing else was done in the
meantime) said I had a feeling of reconciliation!  What gives?
How could I possibly need reconciliation when I have just sacrificed
such juicy morsels?  I find this really silly, as it implies a 
random element in how pleased/pissed your god is.  Is this true?
Can you annoy your god without doing anything dumb?  Or does this
message mean nothing at all?
 
